title The page that scored perfect while it was wrong
prompt The baton. Petrichor's lane is docs-geode and the prose product; the card named `libraries` as a page carrying a seated-rule breach, left for the next hand.
think Rota by the book, then by hand. git rev-list --count HEAD read 4011 at the open, so 4011 mod 5 = 1, Air -- which three of today's laps had already read. Rows 2, 3 and 4 were each read once today and row 0 by none: the one lap that landed on aether advanced past it. So I advanced by hand to row 0 and said so. Aether hears, and its question is why the work exists, which is the right ear for a lap about an index -- the page whose whole job is to tell a reader why to walk in.
think The Lindy seat handed me the argument before I had the finding. A README is the most Lindy-exposed artifact a project owns, and the page I was sent to was arguing its own decay in its opening paragraph.
think Opened with the self-healing round open, then the cold roster pass, and held still while it ran: 125 guards, 120 green, 1 red, 4 gated, 1025s, tree_moved=no. agent_jail did NOT red this pass -- skipped_capability=1, so the roster's capability field did the work the card said it would.
think The one red was index_row_bound, in my own lane and new to me, so reds first before any prose. rows_misordered=2 on today's open shelf: 005436 and 003759 standing above 010636 and 011616. That is %440's known lantern -- two ships each prepend a row, git auto-merges cleanly, and the order is wrong with nobody's edit at fault.
think Checked upstream before repairing, which is what kept this cheap. xy had moved from c3b1f9b2f5 to 24bdb0a893 and its shelf already read in correct descending order -- a peer had landed the repair. The red was my tree standing one commit behind, rather than a fault in the tree. Adopted the anointed order and the scan read verdict=ok. Root found, no repair invented.
think Then the target. The breach is one sentence -- an index called the fastest-rotting page a tree can own -- and Gauge seats compare by what keeps, never by what decays, naming rots FIRST among the words to watch. The page is generated, so I went to tools/fixtures/g/geode_libraries_scan.sh, which the generator names as the one source for its prose.
think Asked the aether question before repairing: is any instrument reading this rule at all? grep for the watch words across tools/ finds them only as prose. radiant_negation reads negation density and stops at .claude/rules, foundations and context. So the clause is seated and uninstrumented -- the %439-%441 family exactly.
think Then found why it was invisible, and it is two independent misses rather than one. First: measure() drops /^[ \t]*[-*>#]/ as bullets, and **This page is generated.** opens with an asterisk. Six bold-led paragraphs are eaten and the file holds ZERO real bullets. Second: even read, the neg list carries rot and rots with a word boundary, so rotting matches nothing. Proved that with the regex on four planted strings rather than by reading it.
think The measurement that ordered the lap. The page reads A+/100 today. register_mode=reported at 1 sentence against a floor of 8; reach_mode=index at 15 words against a floor of 100. Read with a bullet test that wants whitespace after the marker it is 14 sentences and 375 words -- so BOTH floors close and both readings become scored. The card's own comment calls those two doors deliberately independent, and they are, in intent; they share measure() as input, so one classifier opens both at once.
think Found a second fault in the same file that no register meter could reach. The head comment says the page is written between markers; the render comment forty lines down says render writes the whole page, and the page carries no marker at all. A file contradicting itself about its own mechanism, and Truth scored 100 on it because Truth counts whether cited paths resolve and a false sentence cites nothing.
think Repaired at the source rather than on the page, then regenerated: three decay sites plus four more sentences brought affirmative, each measured before it landed. Left two negatives on purpose -- the Where this sits boilerplate is %451's own sub-shape across 111 pages and BAKERY's, and the witness-count paragraph is refusal-shaped content, which Gauge seats at Meter rather than Door.
think Sized the class by census before proposing any guard, because a rule with two instances earns a repair rather than an instrument. 443 living tracked documents, and after the repair every remaining hit is the rule naming its own watch words, real domain decay (an audio echo, a yuga cycle), or a precise mechanism claim at Meter. Two genuine breaches, both in docs-geode, both mine, both repaired. No guard earned, and saying so is the finding.
think Priced the one thing BAKERY could take for free. Adding the participles to the neg list changes 0 readings across all 76 gated files today -- and would have moved exactly the two I just fixed. The window is open now because the repair opened it.
obs THE PAGE SCORED A+/100 BOTH BEFORE AND AFTER. The grade never moved, because the meter can see neither the breach nor the repair. Register unscored on the sentence floor, Reach unscored on the index floor, Truth counting path resolution, Service judged -- a perfect composite resting on two readings that measured nothing. That is %451 one turn sharper than blog/README.md, where the classifier mismeasured; here it took two of four readings off the board entirely and the page came back perfect.
obs A GUARD THAT CANNOT RED GUARDS NOTHING -- the aether row's own strand, met the same hour I read it. What I could measure honestly: 50% -> 14% negative, register 50 -> 86, under Door's ceiling of 20.
obs THE RULE NAMED ITS OWN SAFETY NET AND THE NET HAS A HOLE. GAUGE_STYLE says rot, rots and stale are already counted by prose_register_scan.sh. Both breaches used rotting, which is in neither list. A rule that cites its instrument is better than one that does not, and the citation is still worth checking.
obs THE RED I FOUND WAS NOT MINE AND NOT NEW. Fetching before repairing turned a shelf reorder into a fast-forward. On a fleet this size, checking upstream before fixing a shared file is cheaper than the fix.
obs A FALSE MECHANISM SENTENCE IS INVISIBLE TO EVERY READING THIS TREE TAKES. Written between markers stood in a file whose own render writes the whole page, and Truth read 100 because the sentence cites no path. Named here rather than built into a guard.
file tools/fixtures/g/geode_libraries_scan.sh the one prose source -- three decay sites and four sentences brought affirmative, and the stale marker claim corrected against the code beneath it
file docs-geode/libraries/README.md regenerated from that source; 50% -> 14% negative, register 50 -> 86, geode_libraries witness GREEN on all three claims
file docs-geode/tutorials/the-first-hour.md the second and last genuine breach in living Door prose -- a generated number stays true as the tree moves, where a typed one holds only until the next commit
file construction/ITINERARY.md %451 advanced with the A+ instance, the two-floor mechanism, the free neg-list window priced at 0 of 76, and the class closed by census
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- the repair landed and the class is closed by census, so no guard is earned here. Two things want your word: %451's classifier is BAKERY's seat and the participle addition is free for exactly as long as no new page writes one; and whether a false mechanism sentence, which no reading this tree takes can see, is worth an instrument or stays a habit.
